# Normalize the working tree to LF everywhere, including Windows checkouts.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, so without this a
# Windows checkout rewrites every file to CRLF. `zig fmt --check` compares
# against LF-normalized output and reports all 565 .zig files as unformatted,
# which is exactly how the windows-x86_64 CI job first failed. The same thing
# happens to any contributor cloning on Windows.
#
# The repository is LF throughout already, so this changes no committed bytes;
# it only fixes what lands in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact fixtures and assets: never transform these.
*.gz  binary
*.png binary
*.m4a binary
*.caf binary
